{
  "title": "iOS share extension: stale slow-message timer, double completion, no re-entry guard",
  "description": "ShareViewController.swift: ShareStatus (85-95) is bypassed by errorMessage (only meaningful in .error) and showSlowAffordance (only meaningful in .sending). \
The 10s sleeper Task (274-285) is never stored or cancelled: if attempt 1 fails within 10s and the user taps Try Again, attempt 1's sleeper sees .sending and shows 'Still working' early. \
On success, asyncAfter(1.5) calls onComplete() (305-308) and so does the Done button (133), unguarded, so completeRequest can run twice. .onAppear { checkLoginAndSend() } (145) doesn't check status, so a second onAppear would POST the capture again. \
Want: .sending(slow: Bool) and .failed(String) cases, one stored send Task cancelled on retry, and a once-only completion. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
